WEBVTT

00:35.905 --> 00:37.324
You can't regenerate, can you?

00:38.368 --> 00:41.040
Black Shadow Stone is a cellular alloy

00:41.040 --> 00:43.879
with organelles
that are reinforced by steel.

00:44.673 --> 00:47.846
Meaning that,
so long as you can maintain your organs,

00:47.846 --> 00:49.683
you can regenerate infinitely.

00:50.183 --> 00:53.941
That's why
I destroyed the cells themselves.

00:55.152 --> 00:59.953
The parts of your cells that were crushed
are now nothing but metal.

01:00.872 --> 01:03.126
I'm… a coward.

01:04.170 --> 01:08.637
Scared that my loved ones will get hurt
or that I'll hurt someone else.

01:09.180 --> 01:13.648
That's how scary weapons are,
and that's why I obsess over them…

01:14.649 --> 01:19.200
how to use them, their force,
their effects, their weak points…

01:20.077 --> 01:22.791
My Blooming, "Destruction"…

01:23.375 --> 01:24.795
will smash you to pieces!

01:25.420 --> 01:26.507
SEVEN PUNISHMENTS

01:43.248 --> 01:52.851
MISSION: YOZAKURA FAMILY

03:00.277 --> 03:05.203
PLAN 24
SHION & KENGO VS. CHACHA & AONUMA

03:32.299 --> 03:34.763
That released
the rush of blood in my head.

03:35.221 --> 03:36.349
Thanks, man.

03:41.860 --> 03:44.658
Vajra Splitter!

03:45.075 --> 03:47.496
So glad you took the bait.

03:47.955 --> 03:51.379
Just a second later,
and I would have killed you.

03:52.172 --> 03:56.138
Thanks to that blow of yours,
I didn't end up going on a rampage.

03:56.598 --> 03:59.854
And I was able
to manage my own Blooming.

04:05.156 --> 04:06.283
Shinzo here.

04:06.785 --> 04:08.539
I've secured the route.

04:08.789 --> 04:11.712
<i>Good work! I'm so glad that you're safe!</i>

04:11.878 --> 04:13.924
Hey, is that you, Ayaka?

04:13.924 --> 04:18.976
Turmeric's on a roll. It's all thanks
to your support, Ayaka. Thanks.

04:18.976 --> 04:21.815
I'll be taking the quickest route
to join Taiyo.

04:21.815 --> 04:22.984
There he is!

04:23.151 --> 04:24.403
Get rid of him!

04:24.904 --> 04:27.242
Ugh. They just keep coming!

04:38.389 --> 04:39.308
What?

04:40.393 --> 04:43.650
All of the units embedded
with self-destruct chips…

04:43.650 --> 04:45.361
have been destroyed.

04:46.948 --> 04:50.581
If only we'd implanted them
into all of the test subjects, too…

04:51.499 --> 04:55.508
But, hey, at least we managed
to minimize the risk of any data leaks.

04:56.008 --> 04:57.678
It was only intruders.

04:58.179 --> 05:01.185
Was it really necessary
to lose our valuable samples as well?

05:01.686 --> 05:03.105
It's all good.

05:03.397 --> 05:07.573
As long as the Seed-Sowing Project
succeeds, we won't need anything else.

05:08.366 --> 05:10.245
They exploded.

05:10.245 --> 05:13.502
<i>Kengo here. That was
totally freaky and totally gross.</i>

05:13.502 --> 05:15.046
<i>What's going on here?</i>

05:15.255 --> 05:16.591
Nanao here.

05:16.591 --> 05:19.471
I've spotted a detonation device
embedded in one of the corpses.

05:19.973 --> 05:21.768
Looks like the enemy was behind this.

05:22.060 --> 05:24.816
Uh-huh. Uh-huh. I see.

05:25.275 --> 05:27.195
I get it. Damn them to hell.

05:28.281 --> 05:29.951
Hey, everyone, listen up.

05:29.951 --> 05:31.663
This is the worst news you'll ever hear.

05:32.122 --> 05:36.046
Apparently Kawashita doesn't give a damn
about this hideout or his test subjects.

05:36.673 --> 05:38.050
And it's not just us.

05:38.050 --> 05:41.808
He's planning to bring
even himself down with us, too…

05:42.184 --> 05:44.522
for the sake of his scheme.

05:46.400 --> 05:47.027
KAWASHITA CLINIC

05:47.360 --> 05:51.076
KENJI: I WAS ABLE TO RESTORE IT
After salvaging the transaction data
between Tanpopo and some external sources…

05:51.620 --> 05:54.249
"SEED-SOWING PROJECT"
I was able to restore something
that looks like a plan.

05:55.084 --> 05:58.382
At the deepest part of this hideout,
which doesn't show up in the blueprints,

05:58.382 --> 06:01.681
they've got more than 2,000 tons
of concentrated Hazakura stored.

06:02.390 --> 06:05.146
More than enough
for roughly ten billion people.

06:05.689 --> 06:08.361
The entire storage vault
is covered with explosives…

06:08.987 --> 06:11.868
and the instant the Hazakura
synthesized at the upper level

06:11.868 --> 06:13.830
reaches the vault's max capacity,

06:14.122 --> 06:15.709
the whole hideout will blow up.

06:16.586 --> 06:19.717
Massive amounts of Hazakura
will be released into the ocean.

06:20.886 --> 06:22.640
Judging by the currents in this area,

06:22.640 --> 06:25.436
it will only take a few years
to spread across the ocean surface.

06:25.729 --> 06:29.361
It will seep into the main coastal nations
at a rapid pace.

06:30.739 --> 06:32.868
Only a handful of people
will be compatible.

06:33.285 --> 06:35.624
The majority, unable to tolerate it,
will self-destruct,

06:35.624 --> 06:38.296
while those who aren't fully compatible
will start to go berserk.

06:39.381 --> 06:41.970
We're about to see the start
of natural selection and chaos.

06:43.640 --> 06:45.561
Why would he do that?

06:45.561 --> 06:50.028
He's a doomsday theorist or an anarchist
or a thrill-seeking criminal.

06:50.529 --> 06:52.825
Or maybe something else.

06:53.910 --> 06:56.666
Stopping the Seed-Sowing Project
is now our top priority.

06:57.752 --> 07:00.632
<i>We have an estimated 30 minutes left
before the explosion.</i>

07:01.425 --> 07:02.845
<i>Head out to stop the project</i>

07:02.845 --> 07:05.058
<i>while simultaneously
taking control of the hideout!</i>

07:05.433 --> 07:06.393
Roger that!

07:07.479 --> 07:09.024
I'll blast away the escape hatch.

07:09.650 --> 07:11.487
Not even a single ant will get through!

07:11.863 --> 07:14.577
I'll try to hack
into the detonation system again…

07:15.453 --> 07:19.921
by having my brain waves reflected
in the analysis via electrodes.

07:30.233 --> 07:31.193
Big Sis!

07:32.195 --> 07:34.407
<i>This noise
is the result of reverse-hacking?</i>

07:34.407 --> 07:36.871
<i>If they can interfere
with my brain waves, that means…</i>

07:37.540 --> 07:39.877
What a foolish young girl you are.

07:40.211 --> 07:43.384
To think that you'd take me on
via your brain waves.

07:43.677 --> 07:44.512
Are you okay?

07:44.971 --> 07:46.306
Big Sis, hang in there!

07:46.933 --> 07:49.229
A little jolt like this is nothing.

07:50.524 --> 07:52.987
My hacking system's output is dropping!

07:53.655 --> 07:58.665
I know that you use the enemy's
power sources when you hack…

07:58.999 --> 07:59.959
<i>and so…</i>

08:01.504 --> 08:03.633
<i>all I had to do was shut them down.</i>

08:04.009 --> 08:05.596
Man, what a pain.

08:06.096 --> 08:07.808
<i>Good job freezing the power sources.</i>

08:08.727 --> 08:10.814
AONUMA HAZAKURA EFFICIENCY 366%
Gonna go back to playing tag, okay?

08:11.398 --> 08:15.364
I've shut down every power source
accessible from the outside.

08:15.782 --> 08:19.497
Let me rip you to shreds,
impudent brain and all.

08:19.832 --> 08:21.544
Excessive discharging from the back-flow?

08:21.836 --> 08:22.671
Oh, crap!

08:24.508 --> 08:25.468
Take that.

08:34.820 --> 08:37.743
Whoa, that was close.

08:38.035 --> 08:40.958
Is the system back up, Shion?

08:41.291 --> 08:43.212
Kengo? Why did you--

08:43.212 --> 08:44.674
<i>Huh? What do you mean?</i>

08:44.966 --> 08:48.180
Didn't I hear you say,
"Oh, no, I'm so scared! Save me!"

08:48.180 --> 08:50.017
<i>I never said that! Who would?</i>

08:50.017 --> 08:51.311
<i>Anyway, it's dangerous there.</i>

08:51.311 --> 08:52.146
<i>Out of the way!</i>

08:55.696 --> 08:58.284
No sneaking around, you stupid cat.

09:00.956 --> 09:02.166
Exploding Kengo!

09:03.127 --> 09:05.507
All right, next power source, all of us!

09:05.507 --> 09:08.345
We're going to disrupt them
as we maintain the power sources!

09:08.345 --> 09:11.853
So, Shion, you focus
on demolishing that detonation system!

09:12.186 --> 09:13.314
Don't be ridiculous!

09:13.314 --> 09:14.692
You're not even the combat type!

09:14.692 --> 09:16.946
You'll be out of dolls before you know it!

09:17.322 --> 09:19.702
Don't worry!
I promise you this will work!

09:20.202 --> 09:21.496
<i>Based on what?</i>

09:21.496 --> 09:22.916
-My gut!
-Moron!

09:25.630 --> 09:29.137
You really shouldn't
always think you're right, Shion!

09:29.889 --> 09:32.895
<i>You're the one person I don't need
to tell me that, Mr. Free Spirit!</i>

09:32.895 --> 09:35.107
<i>And you're running out of units!</i>

09:35.399 --> 09:37.863
<i>Yeah, but what about you, Shion?
Telling me to withdraw,</i>

09:37.863 --> 09:40.786
<i>when you have no qualms
about putting yourself at risk?</i>

09:41.537 --> 09:43.290
You've been like that from way back, huh?

09:43.708 --> 09:47.256
Losing your confidence and brooding alone
or turning into a shut-in.

09:47.716 --> 09:51.473
In the end, you can't even see the faces
of your family, who worry about you.

09:51.891 --> 09:55.649
Just like you care about us,
we care about you, too.

09:56.567 --> 10:00.491
<i>You really need to put that
into your calculations, too.</i>

10:01.159 --> 10:03.080
Hey, we're siblings, after all.

10:03.414 --> 10:05.459
<i>Let's enjoy
walking the tightrope together!</i>

10:06.671 --> 10:07.840
Jeez.

10:08.633 --> 10:10.177
You damned fool.

10:11.096 --> 10:15.020
<i>All right, gotcha!
I'm going to guide you, so do as I say!</i>

10:15.271 --> 10:16.607
Huh? Did you just say,

10:16.607 --> 10:20.322
"Thanks for rescuing me!
I can really lean on you, Kengo"?

10:20.322 --> 10:22.118
<i>Damn you, I'm going to tear off your ears!</i>

10:23.120 --> 10:24.456
So annoying.

10:24.957 --> 10:27.170
At this rate,
the power source will be restored.

10:27.588 --> 10:29.884
Should I head back
to shut it down before I kill him?

10:30.217 --> 10:32.346
Don't panic, Aonuma.

10:32.346 --> 10:35.186
<i>Even if you don't stop them completely,</i>

10:35.186 --> 10:37.524
<i>there's only 21 minutes
and 49 seconds left.</i>

10:38.317 --> 10:42.534
If we can hold them off,
it will mean victory for us and our plan.

10:42.743 --> 10:47.293
We're going to neutralize the detonation
system in the next 21 or so minutes!

10:47.586 --> 10:48.462
Copy that!

10:53.765 --> 10:56.228
Shion, you take care of the hacking.

10:56.646 --> 10:58.983
We'll see if we can stop it physically.

11:03.492 --> 11:04.537
They just keep coming!

11:04.870 --> 11:06.707
You're not finishing them off,
Taiyo Asano.

11:11.884 --> 11:14.640
Drop them with one blow.
Don't let them strike back.

11:14.640 --> 11:16.059
R-Right!

11:16.059 --> 11:19.525
From now on, you're getting a body blow
every time you fail to drop them!

11:19.525 --> 11:20.652
R-Right.

11:21.779 --> 11:23.282
We're just practice?

11:25.119 --> 11:26.998
<i>Take a left at the next intersection.</i>

11:27.331 --> 11:29.503
<i>Take the right-hand elevator
up to the 16th floor.</i>

11:29.503 --> 11:31.757
<i>You'll find the power source
as soon as you get off.</i>

11:31.757 --> 11:32.885
Roger!

11:33.427 --> 11:34.304
Huh?

11:34.304 --> 11:36.391
<i>I shut off the lights
so we can throw them off.</i>

11:36.391 --> 11:38.855
<i>The enemy will be
on the right side of the next junction.</i>

11:38.855 --> 11:39.940
Gotcha!

11:41.986 --> 11:42.905
Number five!

11:44.658 --> 11:46.077
<i>That's a good pace.</i>

11:46.077 --> 11:47.038
All right!

11:51.756 --> 11:52.674
Whoa!

11:57.893 --> 12:00.147
Can they see where we are?

12:04.990 --> 12:06.201
How's it looking, Chacha?

12:06.201 --> 12:08.121
<i>According to my sensors,
we've stopped four,</i>

12:08.121 --> 12:10.919
<i>while another four
are heading towards Block Six</i>

12:10.919 --> 12:14.217
<i>on the 16th floor at your 10 o'clock.
Fire in three seconds.</i>

12:14.551 --> 12:15.595
Roger that.

12:22.358 --> 12:25.447
Whoa, his aim is crazy accurate!

12:25.447 --> 12:27.076
We're down to less than 20 bodies now.

12:27.869 --> 12:28.871
Kengo.

12:29.372 --> 12:30.332
Damn.

12:32.128 --> 12:36.762
You're losing because you failed
to grasp how great my mind is.

12:37.263 --> 12:39.727
I pity you, you wretched fools.

12:55.049 --> 12:57.888
So they had you locked up all this time?

12:58.388 --> 13:00.309
They have no idea what they were missing.

13:00.309 --> 13:03.858
Would you like to let the world know
about that brain of yours?

13:04.358 --> 13:09.243
<i>He was the only one
who ever listened to me.</i>

13:10.329 --> 13:15.422
Akai's flames, Kurosawa's steel,
Aonuma's ice--

13:15.422 --> 13:21.519
unlike their crude affectations,
what I possess is pure talent.

13:22.019 --> 13:26.277
I have no problem
seeing all of you.

13:26.737 --> 13:27.697
Give it up.

13:28.198 --> 13:31.496
You're not capable of understanding me.

13:31.496 --> 13:32.749
Oh, yes, I do understand.

13:33.416 --> 13:37.968
That's just how a shut-in who resents not
being recognized by the world would think.

13:38.468 --> 13:40.222
I see that you're just like me.

13:40.765 --> 13:43.311
I do have sympathy for your plight.

13:43.311 --> 13:47.027
But if you look down on those around you
just to validate yourself,

13:47.027 --> 13:52.496
then you're the same as the people
who abandoned you for being useless.

13:53.373 --> 13:55.210
No matter how smart you may be,

13:55.210 --> 13:57.632
if you're narrow-minded,
then you're no more than a fool.

13:58.049 --> 14:01.139
I have no idea
what you're trying to convey,

14:01.139 --> 14:03.435
but it's not as if I'm inclined to listen.

14:03.811 --> 14:05.355
Let me end this now.

14:08.654 --> 14:10.365
<i>We're within the estimated time frame.</i>

14:10.365 --> 14:11.702
<i>Good work, Aonuma.</i>

14:12.202 --> 14:15.208
Grandma always used to say
that working long hours was toxic.

14:15.208 --> 14:17.589
<i>18 minutes and 55 seconds to go.</i>

14:17.589 --> 14:19.718
<i>Let's celebrate in advance. Do it.</i>

14:24.060 --> 14:25.062
Hmm?

14:30.949 --> 14:31.992
A fake?

14:32.493 --> 14:33.955
Aonuma, respond.

14:33.955 --> 14:36.752
<i>-What's going on, Chacha?
-Everything's good over here.</i>

14:36.752 --> 14:38.296
<i>-What's the status?
-Sorry, I lost him.</i>

14:38.296 --> 14:40.300
<i>-Hurry up, and tell me what to do!
-What should I do?</i>

14:40.300 --> 14:41.762
<i>I'm hearing my own voice over and over!</i>

14:41.762 --> 14:44.559
Not good.
It's impossible to identify the enemy.

14:44.977 --> 14:46.104
<i>You'll have to figure it out--</i>

14:46.104 --> 14:47.941
My bad, Chacha. So which one…

14:47.941 --> 14:50.237
<i>Head to the power source
on the tenth floor right now!</i>

14:50.237 --> 14:51.489
<i>Request backup from Kawashita.</i>

14:51.991 --> 14:53.536
<i>Stay right where you are.</i>

14:53.536 --> 14:55.247
<i>Go to Block B on the 11th floor.</i>

14:55.247 --> 14:56.207
<i>Join Kurosawa.</i>

14:56.207 --> 14:58.754
-…is the real you?
<i>-Don't be swayed by fake information!</i>

14:59.130 --> 15:01.885
<i>Head to the corridor leading
to the Research Wing right now.</i>

15:03.388 --> 15:05.935
<i>They're jamming transmissions
with my voice?</i>

15:06.562 --> 15:09.943
During the blackout,
we dressed the Kengo Dolls as Aonuma,

15:10.193 --> 15:13.701
after which I baited you
and hacked into your channel.

15:14.201 --> 15:17.584
At the same time,
Kengo flooded you with fake messages.

15:17.584 --> 15:18.836
When push comes to shove,

15:18.836 --> 15:21.592
it's all about how much you've
been communicating on a daily basis.

15:21.592 --> 15:23.554
No matter how superb
your analytical skills

15:23.554 --> 15:25.015
or how tight your security may be,

15:25.015 --> 15:27.352
unless you look
at the person behind those texts,

15:27.352 --> 15:29.566
that will end up
being your weak point.

15:31.152 --> 15:31.987
There!

15:32.362 --> 15:33.198
Here we go!

15:33.490 --> 15:36.287
Once all of the power sources are on,
we can lock them.

15:36.287 --> 15:38.667
We'll both be at full power for round two.

15:42.091 --> 15:43.468
All right…

15:44.428 --> 15:46.099
let's go, Kengo.

15:46.432 --> 15:48.646
Gotcha, Shion.

15:53.279 --> 15:55.325
Do you know what mirror neurons are?

15:55.952 --> 15:57.287
They say that living creatures

15:57.287 --> 16:00.628
activate the same neurons
as the person they're looking at,

16:00.628 --> 16:02.715
which enables them to feel empathy.

16:02.715 --> 16:04.803
And I'm good at empathizing.

16:04.803 --> 16:07.767
By enhancing it through Blooming,
I can use Assimilation…

16:07.767 --> 16:09.186
right into that person themselves.

16:12.819 --> 16:14.029
My eyes…

16:14.656 --> 16:16.910
Your real name is Ryo Aoyanagi.

16:17.620 --> 16:22.129
Height, 169 cm. Weight, 50 kg. Age, 17.

16:22.129 --> 16:23.591
You're from Shojin City.

16:24.133 --> 16:26.345
Anyone can look that up.

16:26.345 --> 16:29.310
I hope you don't think
that's enough to become me--

16:29.310 --> 16:32.567
That jacket you're always wearing
is a keepsake from Grandma Hako.

16:37.785 --> 16:42.294
After my parents abandoned me,
I ended up living in an alleyway.

16:48.181 --> 16:49.433
This egg's mine!

16:50.268 --> 16:51.437
Oh, crap!

16:51.939 --> 16:53.149
So yummy!

16:53.651 --> 16:55.821
Spit it out, you miserable brat!

16:55.821 --> 16:58.243
Sorry to disappoint you!

16:59.370 --> 17:00.581
Get out of my face, already.

17:00.581 --> 17:02.251
This is my territory.

17:02.251 --> 17:06.092
Like I care! Here, you get
all that warm air coming from inside!

17:07.177 --> 17:09.975
I mean, you're the one
whose days are numbered.

17:09.975 --> 17:12.020
So why don't you leave it
for us younger guys?

17:18.324 --> 17:21.915
All righty, looks like I'm having
brat hot-pot for dinner tonight.

17:21.915 --> 17:24.587
Y-You old witch!

17:38.156 --> 17:41.622
<i>If only she'd just croak already,
then I'd have more room.</i>

17:51.223 --> 17:54.104
<i>What the hell? It's not warm at all.</i>

17:54.606 --> 17:57.570
<i>Is it broken, or are they closed?
It's freezing.</i>

17:58.196 --> 18:01.077
<i>That Grandma Hako,
guess she ran off by herself.</i>

18:01.494 --> 18:03.289
<i>Well, who could blame her?</i>

18:03.832 --> 18:06.838
<i>I'm so screwed, aren't I?</i>

18:07.632 --> 18:10.053
<i>That was a pretty useless life I led.</i>

18:44.455 --> 18:48.171
It was several weeks later
that Kawashita showed up.

18:52.053 --> 18:53.139
Shut up!

18:54.433 --> 18:57.147
Blooming weakens when your soul wavers.

18:57.648 --> 18:59.944
That's not enough to freeze my mouth.

19:01.865 --> 19:05.539
Hey, I get it.
Kindness is a scary thing, huh?

19:05.539 --> 19:11.342
It makes you wonder if there's a catch
or whether you deserve to have it, right?

19:12.219 --> 19:15.266
Since I can change my looks
and my voice at will,

19:15.266 --> 19:18.899
I can't always accept someone's kindness
without questioning it.

19:19.526 --> 19:20.736
But you know what?

19:20.903 --> 19:22.740
There are people
who are just genuinely kind

19:22.740 --> 19:24.744
and would gladly
give up their lives for others,

19:24.744 --> 19:27.207
wonderful idiots like that.

19:27.457 --> 19:29.671
I know that Grandma Hako
was like that, too.

19:29.671 --> 19:30.965
Cut it out.

19:33.344 --> 19:35.766
Come on, she warmed you up, didn't she?

19:36.267 --> 19:39.273
You can't stay frozen with guilt
forever, right?

19:39.774 --> 19:42.822
The memories you shut away,
I'm going to awaken them.

19:49.334 --> 19:52.132
<i>You're not cold, are you? Miserable brat.</i>

20:03.530 --> 20:05.993
I'm warm, Granny.

20:06.536 --> 20:08.372
What are you doing, Aonuma?

20:08.372 --> 20:10.669
Your Hazakura output is plummeting.

20:10.669 --> 20:12.088
Don't let him manipulate you!

20:12.088 --> 20:15.804
<i>Sorry, Chacha. I can't fight anymore.</i>

20:15.804 --> 20:17.015
What did you--

20:18.560 --> 20:20.396
What's this feeling I'm getting?

20:20.898 --> 20:21.942
It's like…

20:22.652 --> 20:24.029
I'm being observed.

20:27.035 --> 20:31.126
Kengo's Blooming is practically a cheat.
Pretty fun to watch, huh?

20:31.126 --> 20:34.759
Compared to that,
my Blooming's a simple thing.

20:36.345 --> 20:37.848
Analyzation.

20:37.848 --> 20:41.815
Specs so high that I can gain
full control of this hideout's system.

20:41.815 --> 20:43.860
Like a kind of supercomputer.

20:44.319 --> 20:46.991
Thanks to Kengo,
I can finally operate at 100%.

20:48.202 --> 20:50.916
And this incident taught me that,
at the end of the day,

20:50.916 --> 20:52.795
human souls and systems are the same.

20:53.337 --> 20:55.551
I also learned all about you.

20:56.093 --> 20:59.767
At this moment, I'd say you were
in the palm of my hand.

21:02.313 --> 21:04.986
So anyway… it's game over.

21:08.660 --> 21:11.958
Me… of all people?

21:14.463 --> 21:16.593
<i>Taiyo? Kyoichiro? My bad.</i>

21:16.593 --> 21:19.181
<i>I just finally managed
to break through the defense system.</i>

21:19.181 --> 21:22.103
<i>I'm relaunching the
"Stop the Seed-Sowing Project" mission.</i>

21:23.272 --> 21:24.399
Roger that.

21:25.569 --> 21:28.240
We've arrived at the gate
to the deepest part of the hideout.

21:28.240 --> 21:31.121
It's going to be a race
to see who can stop them first.

21:32.583 --> 21:35.046
Starting now, we're switching gears
to capture Kawashita.

21:35.046 --> 21:36.633
Get ready, Taiyo.

21:36.633 --> 21:37.551
Right.

21:42.393 --> 21:43.354
Whirlwind.

21:43.354 --> 21:44.565
Ascending Waterfall.

21:52.247 --> 21:53.959
Oh, come on.

21:53.959 --> 21:56.881
That door was custom-built, you know.

22:02.225 --> 22:03.770
Hey there, Taiyo Asano.

22:04.271 --> 22:06.901
Thanks for looking after Hakuja
on the train.

22:07.736 --> 22:08.989
Kawashita!

23:54.407 --> 23:56.036
NEXT TIME
AI AND MIZUKI
